.TH VMSCHED 1
.SH NAME
vmsched \- place Linux guests across hypervisor hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cloud/vmsched
[
.B -n
.I guests
] [
.B -m
.I megabytes
] [
.B -i
.I initrd
] [
.B -s
.I seconds
]
.I bzImage
.I hostdir
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Vmsched
reads each host's
.IB hostdir /dev/vm/host
(see
.IR vm (3))
\(em a host's namespace mounted here, usually over Styx \(em and places
.I guests
machines: on the host running the fewest, ties to the one with the
most contiguous memory, never on one whose largest free run is smaller
than the guest.  Each is then run at once by
.IR vmlinux (1)
in a namespace of its own with its host's
.B /dev
bound in, typed a line naming it and its host, and stopped when it
answers.  Placement is decided here; the hosts only report and obey.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cloud/vmsched.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR vm (3),
.IR vmlinux (1)
.SH BUGS
One placement policy, decided once; nothing migrates or rebalances.
